P2  TOURNAMENTS | score sequence: transitive = UNIQUE realization (0 entropy = rigid) vs regular (max)
========================================================================
  n=3: #classes=2; transitive score (0, 1, 2) realized by 1 class (H=0.00); max fiber=1 at score(s) (0, 1, 2) (H=0.00)
  n=4: #classes=4; transitive score (0, 1, 2, 3) realized by 1 class (H=0.00); max fiber=1 at score(s) (0, 1, 2, 3) (H=0.00)
  n=5: #classes=12; transitive score (0, 1, 2, 3, 4) realized by 1 class (H=0.00); max fiber=3 at score(s) (1, 2, 2, 2, 3) (H=1.58)
  => the TRANSITIVE tournament (score 0..n-1) is the UNIQUE realization: reconstruction entropy 0 = RIGID
     (the AP/nullcone vertex). The largest fiber (near-regular scores) carries the hidden entropy (kps wall).

========================================================================
P3  the DUAL: score-DISTRIBUTION entropy (transitive MAX) vs RECONSTRUCTION entropy (transitive 0)
========================================================================
  n=5: transitive -> score-DIST entropy 2.32 (MAX, spread) but RECONSTRUCTION entropy 0 (unique);
        regular    -> score-DIST entropy -0.00 (MIN, delta)  but RECONSTRUCTION entropy MAX (huge fiber).
  n=7: transitive -> score-DIST entropy 2.81 (MAX, spread) but RECONSTRUCTION entropy 0 (unique);
        regular    -> score-DIST entropy -0.00 (MIN, delta)  but RECONSTRUCTION entropy MAX (huge fiber).
  n=11: transitive -> score-DIST entropy 3.46 (MAX, spread) but RECONSTRUCTION entropy 0 (unique);
        regular    -> score-DIST entropy -0.00 (MIN, delta)  but RECONSTRUCTION entropy MAX (huge fiber).
  => the two entropies are DUAL. The AP/transitive is MAX spread + ZERO hidden info = rigid; the
     regular/Paley pole is MIN spread + MAX hidden info. Rigidity = max-order-yet-uniquely-determined.

========================================================================
P4  REALS | continued-fraction prefix: golden (min = FOIL) vs anti-golden t*=14/183 (max = extremal)
========================================================================
  Khinchin's constant (a.e. geometric mean of partial quotients) ~= 2.6854
  golden [0;1,1,..]: partial quotients [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1], geo-mean 1.000 << Khinchin = WORST-approx (min CF-entropy) = LRC FOIL (S206)
  t* = 14/183 = [0;13,14]: geo-mean 13.491 >> Khinchin = WELL-approx (max CF-entropy) = the extremal
  => the CF 'arithmetic entropy' (info per convergent) is MINIMAL for golden (foil), MAXIMAL for t* (extremal).

========================================================================
P5  NULLCONE | moment depth = certificate entropy: LRC finite (bounded alphabet) vs GMC infinite
========================================================================
  LRC(14): danger count X in {0,..,13} is BOUNDED => the Bonferroni/moment certificate TERMINATES at
           finite detection depth (~5, klein-S389/THM-671): FINITE arithmetic entropy (a finite certificate).
  GMC/NC2: radial degree is UNBOUNDED => no finite moment depth determines the nullcone (Watson/Laplace
           determinacy, S211): INFINITE arithmetic entropy (needs the full radial descent).
  => detection depth = the moment depth at which local data pins the global object = a certificate entropy.

